 \section{Conclusion and Future Work}
-The study combines transparent feature measurements, grouped held-out probes, neighborhood diagnostics and artwork-linked evidence within a mandatory control-gate workflow. Strong release discrimination coexists with encoding leakage and absent verified subjects, so style-conditioned shifts remain descriptive. Frozen ResNet-50 and DINOv2 outperform the handcrafted probe, but none establishes encoding-independent attribution. The contribution is an inspectable atlas and an explicit account of the inference the benchmark cannot support. Future work should capture lossless museum and diffusion originals with common encoding support, verified subject/prompt links and prespecified processing, then evaluate leave-artist, leave-style and unseen-generator holdouts. Dashboard usefulness and material-specific analyses require independent annotations and human evaluation.
